+(defn- stored-collection-in
+  "`values` of cardinality-many `attribute` as a database whose projection is
+  `projection` stores them: `seon.db/stored-collection` over the projection the
+  caller already holds, so a whole population compares against one projection
+  read instead of one per attribute. Known issue: `seon.db/stored-collection-takes-the-projection`."
+  {:malli/schema [:=> [:cat :seon.schema/projection :keyword [:or [:sequential :seon.schema/value] [:set :seon.schema/value]]]
+                  [:or [:vector :seon.schema/value] [:set :seon.schema/value]]]}
+  [projection attribute values]
+  (if (schema.datahike/vector-attribute-in? projection attribute)
+    (vec values)
+    (set values)))
+
